{
	title: '/login claude, API keys from the environment',
	spec: "Each home has its own login (questions.md item 21): `/login claude` runs the Claude subscription OAuth flow as the old Hal did (artifacts old-auth-login.ts, old-login-command.ts): it shows the authorize URL, asks for the code#state value through a secret form question (never stored in history or shown), exchanges it, and writes the tokens to this home's credentials file (paths.authFile, 0600), adding an account or replacing the one with the same email. `/login` without arguments asks which authentication method, then asks for the code or key; its questions stay answerable even when the current turn is blocked on login, and never change the turn's blocked reason (task et). Copied credentials still work; after /login this home refreshes its own tokens, so two homes no longer rotate each other's refresh token away. `/login` with an unknown provider says which ones exist. A session blocked on login (task tf) resumes by itself once the login succeeds. API keys from the environment work for every provider that has one (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for anthropic, as OPENROUTER_API_KEY already does for openrouter) (item 22): a subscription login in the credentials file comes first and the key is the next account, so a user with only a key needs no file at all. Messages that tell the user to log in name /login claude and the variable.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'A session blocked on login is busy, but command questions are data beside the turn, not its state (task et). /login or /login claude can ask there: choosing a method, then answering the code, leaves the turn blocked on login until credentials change; a failed login re-blocks. The prior attempt made command questions the session state and re-derived the state from history after answering, losing the live login reason and refusing the second question as busy.',
		'auth.changed() also resolves when a /login ends (auth.state.logins counts attempts, success or not), so a failed login re-blocks at once instead of showing running until the file changes; a good one resumes within one poll (2s).',
		'The verifier travels as the OAuth state and comes back in code#state, so nothing is kept in memory between the URL and the answer; the question survives restart. The code exchange uses the same token URL as refresh (auth.tokenUrl), so tests fake both with one server; login.profileUrl is the only other endpoint.',
		'The environment key is the account named ANTHROPIC_API_KEY after every file account (auth.all). No file and no key is one error naming both ways to log in (auth.LOG_IN). A file with no anthropic entry is now no accounts, not an error; entries none of which hold a credential still are.',
